    "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:46:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T03:46:54Z",
    "body": "That only matters for multiple changes that occur before the stable state is reached as far as I can tell, and that's what each implementation does. I'm specifically referring to a case like:\n```html\ntrack.mode = \"hidden\";\ntrack.onload = () => track.mode = \"showing\";\n```\n\nThe spec suggests that this should trigger two fetches to the same URL, but that's not what any of the major browsers do.",
